\begin{definition}
(\textbf{Node-interconnector}) It is an interconnector element formulated with a state space representation. This model consists of:

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{State matrix}: Is empty as it does not include state variables.
    \item \textbf{Input vector}: Defined by all currents flowing into the \textit{node-interconnector}.
    \item \textbf{Output vector}: \( \Delta y(t) = [\Delta i^q_{c}, \Delta i^d_{c}] \), where \( i^{q,d}_c \) represents the currents flowing to the capacitor of each \( \pi \)-section line.
