In this paper, we present a simple, effective, and novel nearest point query algorithm based on Voronoi / Delaunay.
For 2D manifold data in 3D, our query speed is 1x-10x faster than KD Tree and R Tree. Even for uniformly distributed random point clouds, our query algorithm achieves speeds comparable to KD Tree.
Our main contributions are as follows:
\begin{itemize}
\item We introduced a concise nearest neighbor search algorithm for 2D manifold point cloud data that significantly improves query speed compared to traditional algorithms.
\item If the point cloud possesses an order, our method can facilitate the identification of the nearest point to \( q \) among \( \{p_i\}_{i=1}^k \), for any \( k \), where \( k \leq n \). This approach can be employed to reduce the time complexity of Density Peak Clustering~\cite{rodriguez2014clustering}, thus enhancing its applicability in large-scale scenarios.
\item Based on our method, we developed a farthest point sampling algorithm with an average complexity of \( O(k \log n) \) in 3D, where \( n \) represents the total number of points and \( k \) denotes the number of samples.
\end{itemize}

