        p_1 & \text{if } m = 1, \\
        \Phi_{m-1}(q) & \text{if } m \neq 1 \land \|q - \Phi_{m-1}(q)\| \leq \|q - p_m\|, \\
        p_m & \text{if } m \neq 1 \land \|q - \Phi_{m-1}(q)\| > \|q - p_m\|,
    \end{cases}
    % }
\end{equation}
which can be understood as a dynamic programming problem, where $\Phi_n(q)$ is the actual nearest point to be extracted. 
Obviously, a na\"{i}ve implementation of the query operation costs $O(n)$ time. In the following, we consider how to boost this implementation.

