\subsection{Fast Query with Elaborated Preprocessing}
%\text{Cell}(\Phi_{m}(q);\mathcal{V}_m)$
Another encouraging finding is that the number of comparisons in our query process, as shown in Table~\ref{table:TestPoints}, can be further reduced, suggesting potential for additional algorithmic acceleration.
Specifically, as previously outlined in our algorithm, when we focus on the time point \(\Phi_{k}(q) = p_k\) during the query process, the current approach only utilizes the information that \( q \in \text{Cell}(\Phi_{k}(q);\mathcal{V}_k) \). 
However, we can infer that \( q \in \cap_{\Phi_i(q) = p_i,1 < i \leq k} \text{Cell}(\Phi_{i-1}(q);\mathcal{V}_{i-1})~\cap~\text{Cell}(\Phi_{k}(q);\mathcal{V}_{k}) \) from the query process.
